      <main id="content"><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianFlipEnergy.compact_count_gaussian_flip_energy_limit"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h1>Actual full Boolean flip-energy Gaussian limit</h1><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianFlipEnergy.compact_count_gaussian_flip_energy_limit</code> · theorem · <a href="index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">For every real C2 compactly supported f, its derivative squared is integrable for the actual centered variance-one Gaussian. The literal normalized counting measure on all N Boolean coordinates integrates the sum of every squared f-value difference under a single-coordinate Boolean flip, including N=0. Its successor full-energy integral converges to four times the Gaussian derivative-square integral. No law, derivative bound, domain or limit certificate is a caller premise.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[\mu_N=2^{-N}\sum_{\varepsilon\in\{0,1\}^N}\delta_\varepsilon,\quad S_N=N^{-1/2}\sum_j\sigma(\varepsilon_j),\quad D_N(\varepsilon)=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\left[f(S_N(\varepsilon^{(j)}))-f(S_N(\varepsilon))\right]^2;\qquad \int D_{N+1}\,d\mu_{N+1}\longrightarrow4\int (f\prime)^2\,d\mathcal N(0,1).\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Derive compact derivative bounds internally</strong><p>C2 gives continuous fprime and differentiable fprime. Its derivative is continuous; both derivative supports are contained in the compact support of f. Compact continuous functions have global bounds. Replace these bounds by their maxima with0. The mean-value bound for the second derivative on the real line gives global K-Lipschitz fprime.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Compute the actual Boolean displacement</strong><p>Subtract the two literal sign sums. Every unmodified coordinate cancels; the flipped coordinate changes its sign by exactly plus or minus2. Thus for N&gt;0 each displacement has magnitude delta=2/sqrt(N), and N delta squared=4. No artificial energy or supplied displacement certificate is used.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Control each true secant and square</strong><p>Apply the real mean-value theorem with the correctly ordered endpoints. For either sign of the displacement, the secant is fprime at an intermediate point within its length of the original point; the equal-endpoint case is handled directly. Both derivative values have magnitude at mostB. Factor the difference of squares to obtain the cubic displacement error.</p></li><li><span>4</span><strong>Sum all coordinates and integrate the uniform error</strong><p>The triangle inequality for the entire finite sum and N delta squared=4 yield the pointwise full-energy error16BK/sqrt(N). The literal count measure has mass1 by positive finite cardinality. Every energy function is genuinely integrable on this finite probability space, including N0. Derivative-observer L1 comes from actual36. The integrable subtraction identity and probability mass1 transfer the same error to the difference of actual integrals.</p></li><li><span>5</span><strong>Pass to the actual factor-four Gaussian limit</strong><p>The scalar inverse square root of the positive successor index tends to0. Squeeze the true integral difference to0. Independently verified36 supplies Gaussian derivative-square L1 and convergence of the same literal count derivative observer. Add four times that limit to the vanishing difference. This proves full-coordinate energy convergence; it supplies no noncompact or cost limit.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>f:Real-&gt;Real, ContDiff Real2 f and HasCompactSupport f are the only analytic premises. Signed f, zero mass and zero f are included.</li><li>The actual canonical finite Boolean carrier and literal cardinal-normalized counting law are fixed, not supplied certificates. Function.update flips exactly one coordinate; full energy is the sum over all coordinates with no one-half.</li><li>C2compact internally supplies nonnegative bounds B,K for derivative and second derivative, hence global derivative Lipschitz control. Genuine finite-count L1 and Gaussian derivative-square L1 are conclusions.</li><li>Only positive successor indices enter the limit. At N0 fullflip energy is an empty sum equal0; the separate derivative observer fprime(0)^2 may be nonzero.</li><li>Authored compact scalar GaussianLSI background, not printed FIRST4.6 or a full GaussianLSI proof. Compact GaussianLSI, finite-Hilbert/noncompact extension, T2, main results and expected costs remain open.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Mathematical proof</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Derive compact derivative bounds internally</h4><p>C2 gives continuous fprime and differentiable fprime. Its derivative is continuous; both derivative supports are contained in the compact support of f. Compact continuous functions have global bounds. Replace these bounds by their maxima with0. The mean-value bound for the second derivative on the real line gives global K-Lipschitz fprime.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[|f\prime(x)|\le B,\quad |f\prime(y)-f\prime(x)|\le K|y-x|,\qquad B,K\ge0.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>compact_derivative_bounds; HasCompactSupport.deriv; HasCompactSupport.exists_bound_of_continuous; ContDiff.deriv&#x27;; ContDiff.differentiable_deriv_two; Convex.norm_image_sub_le_of_norm_deriv_le</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>2. Compute the actual Boolean displacement</h4><p>Subtract the two literal sign sums. Every unmodified coordinate cancels; the flipped coordinate changes its sign by exactly plus or minus2. Thus for N&gt;0 each displacement has magnitude delta=2/sqrt(N), and N delta squared=4. No artificial energy or supplied displacement certificate is used.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[s_j=S_N(\varepsilon^{(j)})-S_N(\varepsilon)=-2\sigma(\varepsilon_j)/\sqrt N,\quad |s_j|=\delta_N=2/\sqrt N,\quad N\delta_N^2=4.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>flip_displacement; flip_distance; Function.update_of_ne; Finset.sum_eq_single; Real.sq_sqrt; hr/hdist</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>3. Control each true secant and square</h4><p>Apply the real mean-value theorem with the correctly ordered endpoints. For either sign of the displacement, the secant is fprime at an intermediate point within its length of the original point; the equal-endpoint case is handled directly. Both derivative values have magnitude at mostB. Factor the difference of squares to obtain the cubic displacement error.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[f(y)-f(x)=a(y-x),\quad |a|\le B,\quad |a-f\prime(x)|\le K|y-x|;\quad |[f(y)-f(x)]^2-(f\prime(x))^2(y-x)^2|\le2BK|y-x|^3.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>bounded_secant; squared_increment_error; exists_deriv_eq_slope; abs_add_le; abs_mul; mul_le_mul</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>4. Sum all coordinates and integrate the uniform error</h4><p>The triangle inequality for the entire finite sum and N delta squared=4 yield the pointwise full-energy error16BK/sqrt(N). The literal count measure has mass1 by positive finite cardinality. Every energy function is genuinely integrable on this finite probability space, including N0. Derivative-observer L1 comes from actual36. The integrable subtraction identity and probability mass1 transfer the same error to the difference of actual integrals.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[|D_N(\varepsilon)-4(f\prime(S_N(\varepsilon)))^2|\le16BK/\sqrt N;\quad\left|\int D_N\,d\mu_N-4\int(f\prime\circ S_N)^2\,d\mu_N\right|\le16BK/\sqrt N.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>full_flip_pointwise_error; countLaw_probability; Integrable.of_finite; hi/iE/iD; integral_sub; integral_const_mul; norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>5. Pass to the actual factor-four Gaussian limit</h4><p>The scalar inverse square root of the positive successor index tends to0. Squeeze the true integral difference to0. Independently verified36 supplies Gaussian derivative-square L1 and convergence of the same literal count derivative observer. Add four times that limit to the vanishing difference. This proves full-coordinate energy convergence; it supplies no noncompact or cost limit.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\int D_{N+1}\,d\mu_{N+1}=e_N+4\int(f\prime\circ S_{N+1})^2\,d\mu_{N+1},\quad e_N\to0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad4\int(f\prime)^2\,d\gamma.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>GaussianCompactEntropy.compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits; tr/te/tC; Real.tendsto_sqrt_atTop; tendsto_inv_atTop_zero; squeeze_zero_norm; Tendsto.add</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h2>Lean verification</h2><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianFlipEnergy.compact_count_gaussian_flip_energy_limit"><summary>Lean statement · compact_count_gaussian_flip_energy_limit</summary><p>For every real C2 compactly supported f, its derivative squared is integrable for the actual centered variance-one Gaussian. The literal normalized counting measure on all N Boolean coordinates integrates the sum of every squared f-value difference under a single-coordinate Boolean flip, including N=0. Its successor full-energy integral converges to four times the Gaussian derivative-square integral. No law, derivative bound, domain or limit certificate is a caller premise.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem compact_count_gaussian_flip_energy_limit
    (f : ℝ → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f) (hs : HasCompactSupport f) :
    let μ : (n : ℕ) → Measure (Fin n → Bool) := fun n =&gt;
      (Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ • Measure.count
    let S : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → Bool) → ℝ := fun n ε =&gt;
      (Real.sqrt (n : ℝ))⁻¹ * ∑ j : Fin n, if ε j then (1 : ℝ) else -1
    let γ : Measure ℝ := gaussianReal 0 1
    Integrable (fun x =&gt; (deriv f x)^2) γ ∧
    (∀ n : ℕ, Integrable
      (fun ε : Fin n → Bool =&gt; ∑ j : Fin n,
        (f (S n (Function.update ε j (!ε j))) - f (S n ε))^2) (μ n)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt; ∫ ε : Fin (n+1) → Bool,
      (∑ j : Fin (n+1),
        (f (S (n+1) (Function.update ε j (!ε j))) - f (S (n+1) ε))^2)
      ∂μ (n+1)) atTop (𝓝 (4 * ∫ x, (deriv f x)^2 ∂γ))</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gaussianflipenergy.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianFlipEnergy.compact_count_gaussian_flip_energy_limit"><summary>Lean proof · compact_count_gaussian_flip_energy_limit</summary><p>Derive compact derivative bounds internally; Compute the actual Boolean displacement; Control each true secant and square; Sum all coordinates and integrate the uniform error; Pass to the actual factor-four Gaussian limit</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem compact_count_gaussian_flip_energy_limit
    (f : ℝ → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f) (hs : HasCompactSupport f) :
    let μ : (n : ℕ) → Measure (Fin n → Bool) := fun n =&gt;
      (Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ • Measure.count
    let S : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → Bool) → ℝ := fun n ε =&gt;
      (Real.sqrt (n : ℝ))⁻¹ * ∑ j : Fin n, if ε j then (1 : ℝ) else -1
    let γ : Measure ℝ := gaussianReal 0 1
    Integrable (fun x =&gt; (deriv f x)^2) γ ∧
    (∀ n : ℕ, Integrable
      (fun ε : Fin n → Bool =&gt; ∑ j : Fin n,
        (f (S n (Function.update ε j (!ε j))) - f (S n ε))^2) (μ n)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt; ∫ ε : Fin (n+1) → Bool,
      (∑ j : Fin (n+1),
        (f (S (n+1) (Function.update ε j (!ε j))) - f (S (n+1) ε))^2)
      ∂μ (n+1)) atTop (𝓝 (4 * ∫ x, (deriv f x)^2 ∂γ)) := by
  change Integrable (fun x =&gt; (deriv f x)^2) (gaussianReal 0 1) ∧
    (∀ n, Integrable (flipEnergy f n) (countLaw n)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n =&gt; ∫ ε, flipEnergy f (n+1) ε ∂countLaw (n+1)) atTop
      (𝓝 (4 * ∫ x, (deriv f x)^2 ∂gaussianReal 0 1))
  rcases GaussianCompactEntropy.compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits f hf hs
    with ⟨_, _, iC, jC, _, _, tC, _⟩
  change Tendsto (fun n =&gt; ∫ ε, (deriv f (normalizedSum (n+1) ε))^2 ∂countLaw (n+1))
    atTop (𝓝 (∫ x, (deriv f x)^2 ∂gaussianReal 0 1)) at tC
  have iE (n : ℕ) : Integrable (flipEnergy f n) (countLaw n) := Integrable.of_finite
  have iD (n : ℕ) : Integrable (fun ε =&gt; (deriv f (normalizedSum n ε))^2) (countLaw n) :=
    (jC n).2.2
  obtain ⟨B, K, hB0, hK0, hB, hK⟩ := compact_derivative_bounds f hf hs
  have hi (n : ℕ) :
      ‖(∫ ε, flipEnergy f (n+1) ε ∂countLaw (n+1)) -
        4 * (∫ ε, (deriv f (normalizedSum (n+1) ε))^2 ∂countLaw (n+1))‖ ≤
        16 * B * K * (Real.sqrt ((n+1 : ℕ) : ℝ))⁻¹ := by
    rw [← integral_const_mul, ← integral_sub (iE (n+1)) ((iD (n+1)).const_mul 4)]
    have hp (ε : Fin (n+1) → Bool) :
        ‖flipEnergy f (n+1) ε - 4 * (deriv f (normalizedSum (n+1) ε))^2‖ ≤
          16 * B * K * (Real.sqrt ((n+1 : ℕ) : ℝ))⁻¹ := by
      simpa only [flipEnergy, Real.norm_eq_abs] using
        full_flip_pointwise_error f (hf.differentiable (by norm_num)) B K hB0 hK0 hB hK
          (n+1) (Nat.succ_pos n) ε
    have h := norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const (μ := countLaw (n+1))
      (Filter.Eventually.of_forall hp)
    simpa only [measureReal_def, measure_univ, ENNReal.toReal_one, mul_one] using h
  have tr : Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt; (Real.sqrt ((n+1 : ℕ) : ℝ))⁻¹) atTop (𝓝 0) :=
    tendsto_inv_atTop_zero.comp
      (Real.tendsto_sqrt_atTop.comp
        (tendsto_natCast_atTop_atTop.comp (tendsto_add_atTop_nat 1)))
  have te : Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt;
      (∫ ε, flipEnergy f (n+1) ε ∂countLaw (n+1)) -
        4 * (∫ ε, (deriv f (normalizedSum (n+1) ε))^2 ∂countLaw (n+1)))
      atTop (𝓝 0) := squeeze_zero_norm hi (by simpa using tr.const_mul (16*B*K))
  have t := te.add (tC.const_mul 4)
  simp only [zero_add, sub_add_cancel] at t
  exact ⟨iC, iE, t⟩

end AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianFlipEnergy</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gaussianflipenergy.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><details class="reader-ledger boundary-ledger"><summary>Scope and omitted-condition boundaries</summary><ul><li>Authored compact C2 scalar full literal Boolean coordinate-flip energy limit. Same actual count/card/signsum and Gaussian variance1; internally produced derivative-square Gaussian L1, allN full-energy L1 including0, and successor full energy integral limit4. No supplied law/Lip/bound/domain/limit/mass certificate. GaussianLSI, finiteHilbert/noncompact actual SPHMC square-root extension,T2/FIRST4.6/main/work/composition remain OPEN. Focused3163PASS: genuine N0 fullflip domain/zero energy and N1 actual atoms with no half factor; three standard axioms only. Independent wholeproof/blind/source/exactcommit and shared publication remain separate.</li></ul></details><details class="proof-reader-provenance reader-ledger"><summary>Sources, dependencies, and reuse</summary><h2>Source and reuse</h2><h3>Samplinglib parents called</h3><ul><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gaussiancompactentropy-compact-count-gaussian-entropy-limits.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianCompactEntropy.compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits</code></a></li></ul><h3>Mathlib API called (external library)</h3><ul><li>HasCompactSupport.deriv</li><li>HasCompactSupport.exists_bound_of_continuous</li><li>ContDiff.deriv&#x27;</li><li>ContDiff.differentiable_deriv_two</li><li>Convex.norm_image_sub_le_of_norm_deriv_le</li><li>exists_deriv_eq_slope</li><li>Finset.sum_eq_single</li><li>Finset.abs_sum_le_sum_abs</li><li>MeasureTheory.Integrable.of_finite</li><li>MeasureTheory.integral_sub</li><li>MeasureTheory.integral_const_mul</li><li>MeasureTheory.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const</li><li>Real.tendsto_sqrt_atTop</li><li>tendsto_inv_atTop_zero</li><li>squeeze_zero_norm</li></ul><h3>Mathematical sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.E6">FIRST S4.E6 GaussianLSI background; SLT GaussianPoincare/Limit.lean L592-L1123 full shift-energy route, especially L1030-L1034 factor4; authored actual Boolean secant alternative</a> — Authored compact C2 scalar full literal Boolean coordinate-flip energy limit. Same actual count/card/signsum and Gaussian variance1; internally produced derivative-square Gaussian L1, allN full-energy L1 including0, and successor full energy integral limit4. No supplied law/Lip/bound/domain/limit/mass certificate. GaussianLSI, finiteHilbert/noncompact actual SPHMC square-root extension,T2/FIRST4.6/main/work/composition remain OPEN. Focused3163PASS: genuine N0 fullflip domain/zero energy and N1 actual atoms with no half factor; three standard axioms only. Independent wholeproof/blind/source/exactcommit and shared publication remain separate.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d/Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/Deriv/MeanValue.lean#L152">Pinned actual real mean-value theorem</a> — Reused compiled primitive; endpoint and domain adapters internally proved.</li></ul><p>Samplinglib prose is not a quotation or a source-equivalence certificate. Definitions and aliases are explained as constructions, not counted as new mathematical proofs.</p></details></article></main>
